  (history ("claude" "2026-09-28" "Glasswood SOUND: the fixed moment at the Frozen Tarn (still: 8). Frozen lakes really sing: as the ice flexes, tones whistle and fall. It starts from that sound (soft bells sliding down about an octave in a quarter second, at irregular times), and becomes a slow chorale of bells on the ice over a D pedal in D Lydian: D, E/D, D, C#m/D, E/D, D, the melody leaning on G# and resolving to A (H3). The whistles come back faintly as the last chord rings; a silent 6 s pattern lets it ring out.")))
